+## Qwen3.8 complete DFlash2 round benchmark
+
+`ginfer_qwen3_8_27b_dflash2_round_bench` drives the registered
+`qwen3.8-27b/nvfp4-dflash2-q4` target through consecutive production Program rounds. It holds the
+learned proposal at `K=4`, leaves adaptive context-copy verification through `K=15` intact, uses
+stochastic sampling, CUDA Graphs, INT8-G64 KV, and a fixed 131,072-token shared capacity. A measured
+round includes confirmed-context append, the five-layer Q4 proposal and selector, NVFP4 target
+verification, stochastic acceptance, state commit, and host publication:
+
+```bash
+cmake --build build --parallel \
+  --target ginfer_qwen3_8_27b_dflash2_round_bench
+./build/bench/ginfer_qwen3_8_27b_dflash2_round_bench \
+  --artifact out/qwen3_8_27b_nvfp4_dflash2_q4.ginfer \
+  --context 8192 --batch 8 --warmup 5 --reps 31
+```
+
+Run separate invocations for the resident-context concurrency matrix and the single-request long
+context. The benchmark reserves the worst-case 16 licensed outputs for every round and rejects
+configurations whose page-rounded request entitlements exceed the fixed shared capacity.
+`--profile-measured` requires `--reps 1` and brackets only the measured production round with
+`cudaProfilerStart/Stop`.
+
